feat: Spectral Quantification Pipeline initial implementation

Stack: PostgreSQL 15, Airflow 2.8.1, dbt-postgres 1.8, scikit-learn, FastAPI, Streamlit

Bronze: PostgreSQL FLOAT[] arrays for raw XRF spectra (1801 channels, 0.05 step).
Synthetic WDXRF 300 samples: 60 unary + 120 binary + 120 ternary.
Elements Na/Mg/Al/Fe/Si/P with Gaussian peaks and inter-element matrix effects.

Silver (dbt): UNNEST(FLOAT[]) WITH ORDINALITY converts arrays to long format per channel.

Gold (dbt): fact_spectral_peaks with background-subtracted net intensities,
fact_sample_summary with concentration labels and spectral statistics for PLS.

ML: PLS2 regression, n_components=15 selected by 5-fold RMSECV, R2 > 0.999 all elements.

API: POST /predict returns element concentrations, GET /model/metrics, GET /samples.
DAG: ingest_bronze >> dbt_run >> dbt_test >> train_pls, weekdays 07:00 UTC.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
